SELECTORS IN CSS:

.Basic selectord of css:

selectors{
    property: value;
}
eg:
h1{
    color:green;
}

i.UNIVERSAL SELECTOR:
To select everything in the document.

    universal selector --> * {
                          property:value;
                        }

ii.ELEMENT SELECTOR:
Selects all element of the same type.              

   element selector--> h1,h2 {
                        property:value;
                    }                     
iii.ID SELECTOR:
Selects an element based on the value of an element's id attributes.
>generlly, one element have one unique id (same id not prefer but can)
    
        id selector --> #myid{
                             property:value;
                          } 

iv.CLASS SELECTOR:
Select an elment based on their class attributes.
>we can give different elment same class.

        class selector --> .myclass{
                             property:value;
                            } 

*.DESCENDANT SELECTOR:
>descendant ->parent

EG. Selects all paragraph inside the divs or class or id .     
                            
descendant selector --> div p {
                            property:value;
                        }

                        
*.ADJACENT SIBLING COMBINATOR:
Eg-Heading3 that comes imediately after any paragraph.
>effect on that  just come after elment.

sibling combinator --> p + h3 {
                               property:value;
                            }


*.CHILD COMBINATOR:
Eg.Selects all buttons which are direct children of spans.

child combinator --> span > button {
                                     property:value;
                                }
   
                                
v.ATTRIBUTE SELECTOR:     

Select element based on the presence or value of a given attribute

attribute selector --> input [att="value"]{
                                         property:value;
                                        }

PSEUDO CLASS :
A keyword added to a selector  that specifies a special state of the selected element(s).                   

        :hover       -->when a mouse hover
        :active      -->when a button is clicked
        :checked     -->when a radio button is checked
        :nth-of-type -->select nth term or element

PSEUDO ELEMENT:
A keyword added to a selector that lets you style a SPECIFIC PART of the selected element(s).

        ::first-letter
        ::first-line
        ::selection --> when we select the sentences on a page


CSS:CASCADING STYLESHEETS:

    cascading --> this property always apply on same element and  always last apply.

    What is cascade in css?
    The css cascade algorithm's job is to select CSS declarations in order to determine the correct values for css properties.

    Eg:

    h2{
        background-color:yellow;
    }
     h2{
        background-color:green;
    }
    i.e final green color will be applied.

    SELECTOR SPECIFICITY:

    What is specificity?
    specificity is a algorithm that calculates the weight that is applied given css declaration.
    ___                 _________               ________
    id   class,attributes & pseudo-class   element & pseudo element

    Eg:
         h2{
            background-color:yellow;
        }


    _0__                 ____0_____               ____1____
    id   class,attributes & pseudo-class   element & pseudo element 

    .myclass:hover{
            background-color:yellow;
        }


        _0__                 ____2_____               ____0____
        id   class,attributes & pseudo-class   element & pseudo element 

    What to remember?
    1. id > class > element
    2. more selector > less selector
    3.if specificity is same -->cascading is applied

    Inline specificity
    inline styles are more specific than id. 


     ____             ___                 _________               ________
    inline style      id   class,attributes & pseudo-class   element & pseudo element


!important:
To show the most specific thing in document.
    h2{
             background-color:yellow !important;
         }


INHERITANCE IN CSS:
>transform from upper generation to lower generation.
>button,input not inherit a property by itself 
    eg;
        input{
            background-color: inherit;
        }
>weidth,height,border etc are inherit.